Project 1: A My Shell Program

Name:
myshell - c shell with basic built in commands and external command execution

Synopsis:
myshell

Description:
This project is a command line shell written in c. It supports built in commands such as "mycd" and "mydir" as well as the execution of external system programs using fork() and execvp. The command line prompt contains the pathname followed by > and displays as: "currentdir>"

Files Included:
        myshell.c
        readme
        makefile
	manual
	typescript

How to Compile:
        1. gcc -o myshell myshell.c
        2. make myshell

How to Run:
        ./myshell

Known Bugs:
        N/A

Built-In Commands:
	mycd <directory> - changes the current active directory. If <directory> is left empty, 
	the current directory is displayed. 
		Use: currentdir> mycd newdir
	 	     newdir>
		
		Use: currentdir> mycd
		     currentdir

	myclr - clears the screen
		Use: currentdir> myclr

	mydir <directory> - list the contents of <directory>. If <directory> is empty list contents 
	of current directory.
		Use: currentdir> mydir newdir
		     new_file1  new_file2  new_file3
		
		Use: currentdir> mydir
		     file1  file2  file3

	myenviron - list all environment variables.
		Use: currentdir> myenviron
		     environment variables

	myecho <comment> - echoes <comment> back to the screen.
		Use: currentdir> myecho Hello!
		     Hello!

	myhelp - displays readme with the more tag.
		Use: currentdir> myhelp
		     readme information
		     More...

	mypause - pauses the shell until the "enter" key is pressed.
		Use: currentdir> "mypause"
		     Press [Enter] to continue...

	myquit - exits shell.
		Use: currentdir> myquit

External Commands:
All external commands can be entered into the shell as normal commands and will be executed in a child process using execvp.

Environment Variables:
myshell uses the following environment variables
	shell: stores the absolute pathname of the running shell
	parent: inherited by child process to track the parent shell
	PWD: tracks the current working directory

